WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:02.009
Serving unschooling families in a public

1
00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:04.480
charter school brings distinct challenges,

2
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.969
primarily centered around school compliance expectations.

3
00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:11.390
Unschooling learning happens dynamically through play,

4
00:00:12.159 --> 00:00:12.369
conversation,

5
00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:14.359
and real-world experiences.

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.079
Because families rarely use traditional workbooks or worksheets,

7
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.280
collecting a tangible work sample every learning period

8
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.719
can feel unnatural or intrusive to them.

9
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.569
Unschooling students often learn in nonlinear.

10
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.440
Bursts,

11
00:00:27.639 --> 00:00:30.920
deep diving into one passion like history for weeks

12
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.380
while temporarily pausing formal instruction in other subjects,

13
00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:38.240
or pursuing interests that don't seem to align with state standards.

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.240
This can make it difficult for a teacher

15
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.069
to connect learning with grade level expectations.

16
00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:46.590
Families often reject rigid scope and sequence guides,

17
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.119
prepackaged textbooks,

18
00:00:48.189 --> 00:00:49.400
and state testing,

19
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.220
viewing them as disruptions to their child's natural learning flow.

20
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.610
The term unschooling often gets used as a convenient blanket term

21
00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:01.599
for families who aren't actually delivering instruction or supporting learning.

22
00:01:02.049 --> 00:01:04.510
Because unschooling lacks traditional benchmarks,

23
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.720
it can be tricky to confirm that real learning is happening.

24
00:01:08.089 --> 00:01:10.239
Teachers must verify that the child is

25
00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:12.930
actively supported in a rich learning environment.

26
00:01:13.209 --> 00:01:14.930
Distinguishing thriving,

27
00:01:14.959 --> 00:01:16.550
self-directed exploration

28
00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.639
from passive stagnation or a lack of instruction.

29
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:20.720
Ultimately,

30
00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:24.230
the challenge for charter teachers is maintaining state compliance

31
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.309
and safeguarding student progress

32
00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:30.349
without micromanaging the family's philosophy or creating friction.